<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madho Rao Scindia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Madho Rao Scindia I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madho Rao Scindia was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Gwalior from 1886 to 1925, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jayajirao-scindia">Jayajirao Scindia</a>. He modernised the state's administration and promoted railways, industry, schools and irrigation, including the narrow-gauge Gwalior Light Railway. He was a close ally of British rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and one of the leading princes of his time.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madho-rao-scindia.jpg" alt="Madho Rao Scindia" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madhavrao_Shinde,_GCSI,_GCVO.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
